<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Counting license plate arrangements and ordered interview selections</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>(a)</b> A license plate consists of \({@pnletters@}\) distinct letters followed by \({@pndigits@}\) distinct digits. How many such plates are possible?</p>
<p>Number of plates = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><b>(b)</b> A group of \({@pn2@}\) friends is choosing \({@pr2@}\) of themselves to be interviewed, one after another. In how many orders can they be chosen?</p>
<p>Number of orders = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>Because order matters and no item is repeated in either situation, use the permutation formula:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_nP_r = \frac{n!}{(n - r)!}\)</p>

<p><b>Part (a): License plates with {@pnletters@} distinct letters and {@pndigits@} distinct digits</b><br>
Calculate the number of ordered arrangements for the \({@pnletters@}\) letters chosen from \(26\) letters, and for the \({@pndigits@}\) digits chosen from \(10\) digits (\(0\)–\(9\)):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \text{Letters: } {}_{26}P_{{@pnletters@}} = \frac{26!}{(26 - {@pnletters@})!} = \frac{26!}{{@remL@}!} = \frac{{@numL_factors@} \times {@remL@}!}{{@remL@}!} = {@numL_factors@} = {@pL@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \text{Digits: } {}_{10}P_{{@pndigits@}} = \frac{10!}{(10 - {@pndigits@})!} = \frac{10!}{{@remD@}!} = \frac{{@numD_factors@} \times {@remD@}!}{{@remD@}!} = {@numD_factors@} = {@pD@}\)</p>
<p>By the Fundamental Counting Principle, because both parts of the plate are chosen together, multiply the two counts:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle \text{Total plates} = {@pL@} \times {@pD@} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Number of plates} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part (b): Choosing {@pr2@} friends in order from {@pn2@} friends</b><br>
Substitute \(n = {@pn2@}\) and \(r = {@pr2@}\) into the permutation formula, expand \({@pn2@}!\) down to \({@rem2@}!\), and cancel \({@rem2@}!\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle {}_{{@pn2@}}P_{{@pr2@}} = \frac{{@pn2@}!}{({@pn2@} - {@pr2@})!} = \frac{{@pn2@}!}{{@rem2@}!} = \frac{{@num2_factors@} \times {@rem2@}!}{{@rem2@}!} = {@num2_factors@} = {@ta2@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Number of orders} = {@ta2@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
